{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You shall utterly destroy it and all that is in it</b> — \"it\" refers to the men who were incited. \"And all that is in it\" refers to the women who were drawn after the men. But the little ones — minors, both male and female — are not put to death. And so they said in the Sifrei: Hanan says, \"Fathers shall not be put to death for children\" (Deuteronomy 24:16) — the verse speaks of the incited city. But in the Tosefta of tractate Sanhedrin (14:1) they disputed concerning this: the minor children of the men of the incited city who were incited along with it are not killed; Rabbi Eliezer says: they are killed. Rabbi Akiva said to him: How do I fulfill \"and He will grant you compassion and be compassionate toward you and multiply you\" (Deuteronomy 13:18)? If this refers to having compassion on the adults, has it not already been stated, \"You shall utterly destroy it and all that is in it and its livestock\"? So how do I fulfill \"and be compassionate toward you and multiply you\"? These are the minors within it, etc. Now behold, all these commandments are an explanation of what is stated in the Torah (Exodus 22:19), \"He who sacrifices to elohim shall be destroyed,\" and now Scripture explains what the destruction is in the case of those who incite and those who worship:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The citation of Exodus 22:19 follows the verse numbering in Hebrew Bibles (תשרי parashat Mishpatim); in many English Bibles this is Exodus 22:20."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:15.603690410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}